32fdda9e5a8d3bc62/README.md"},"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/UI-MOPD/Uni-GUI-Desktop-1"}],"name":"Uni-GUI-Desktop-1","notes":"The UI-MOPD paper builds Uni-GUI from self-collected desktop and mobile trajectories plus cleaned OpenCUA and OpenMobile trajectories; its composition table rounds the self-collected desktop part to about 7K trajectories and 95K steps, so this repository (2,685 trajectories and about 36K steps per the card) holds a portion of it. Per the paper, desktop queries were generated with Kimi-K2.6 from functional points of initialized OSWorld environments, Kimi-K2.6 produced the rollouts and Gemini-3.1-Pro cleaned them, so these are not human demonstrations. Every folder name ends in an OSWorld task ID: a script over the manifest finds 245 distinct IDs, all present in OSWorld's test_all.json, with up to 19 trajectories each. Two opened task.json files for the same OSWorld task label it 'OSWorld'; one repeats that task's instruction verbatim and the other paraphrases it, so the data overlaps OSWorld's test tasks. Both carry verified: false and task_completed: true, while the card's example shows verified: true; 160 folders also hold a result.txt. Linux is inferred from the paper's use of OSWorld environments and the Linux terminal and /home/user paths in the opened queries. Apache-2.0 is the card's declaration and does not cover third-party application content in screenshots. Only two task.json files and one result.txt were opened.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.04425v1","target_id":"github:xlang-ai/osworld","type":"uses"},{"evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/UI-MOPD/Uni-GUI-Desktop-1/raw/92ef5917cd46a899a13461532fdda9e5a8d3bc62/README.md","target_id":"arxiv:2607.04425","type":"documented_by"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Desktop trajectories from the UI-MOPD training data, collected in OSWorld environments: 2,685 tasks across 10 app categories with step screenshots, reasoning traces, normalized actions and pyautogui code.","task_classes":["R04.03.01.01","R06.02.01.02","R11.01.01.01"],"topics":["data-generation","imitation-learning","cross-app"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/UI-MOPD/Uni-GUI-Desktop-1"}
